        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "The body and the `message` field are never printed, and the URL, token, and exception text are kept out of the log, but `error` and `request_id` are logged whenever they pass a character-class whitelist, so an unvetted CRM value like a plain name or digit string would still reach the public log."
